{"id":"g.math.lines-angles.3.9034877b62","section":"math","domain":"geometry","skill":"lines-angles","difficulty":3,"tmpl":"math_hard.similar_triangles_parallel","prompt":"In triangle $ABC$, point $D$ lies on $\\overline{AB}$ and point $E$ lies on $\\overline{AC}$ so that $\\overline{DE}$ is parallel to $\\overline{BC}$. If $AD = 6$, $DB = 12$, and $DE = 15$, what is the length of $\\overline{BC}$?","answer":["45"],"explanation":"Because $\\overline{DE} \\parallel \\overline{BC}$, triangle $ADE$ is similar to triangle $ABC$. So $\\dfrac{DE}{BC} = \\dfrac{AD}{AB} = \\dfrac{6}{18}$. Note that $AB = AD + DB = 18$, not $12$. Then $BC = 15 \\cdot \\dfrac{18}{6} = 45$."},
{"id":"g.math.lines-angles.3.624308538b","section":"math","domain":"geometry","skill":"lines-angles","difficulty":3,"tmpl":"math_hard.similar_triangles_parallel","prompt":"In triangle $ABC$, point $D$ lies on $\\overline{AB}$ and point $E$ lies on $\\overline{AC}$ so that $\\overline{DE}$ is parallel to $\\overline{BC}$. If $AD = 3$, $DB = 4$, and $DE = 10$, what is the length of $\\overline{BC}$?","answer":["70/3"],"explanation":"Because $\\overline{DE} \\parallel \\overline{BC}$, triangle $ADE$ is similar to triangle $ABC$. So $\\dfrac{DE}{BC} = \\dfrac{AD}{AB} = \\dfrac{3}{7}$. Note that $AB = AD + DB = 7$, not $4$. Then $BC = 10 \\cdot \\dfrac{7}{3} = \\frac{70}{3}$."}
